From 928f270baa1df8ac69e765036332f78a59d257e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eicke Hecht <eicke.hecht@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:51:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] zynqmp-r5-echo: r5-1 feature to run on R5_1

Both R5s of a split-mode cluster can run the echo at once; --features
r5-1 builds the firmware for R5_1: its IPI channel (2, 0xFF320000,
RPU GIC interrupt 66, routed to CPU interface 1) and rproc_1_fw_image
(0x3EF00000) for the resource table and trace buffer, with its vrings
and a 512 KiB buffer pool after it, so both cores' shared memory stays in
the one uncached MPU window. build.rs writes memory.x from memory.x.in
with the DDR regions moved; the template is renamed because ld finds an
INCLUDEd memory.x in the package directory before any -L path.

The firmware also brings its own reset handler: aarch32-rt's default
one takes the core ID from MPIDR and parks every core but 0, which kept
R5_1 (affinity 1) spinning in _asm_default_secondary_core_park. In split
mode each R5 runs its own image from its own TCMs, so it always starts
up as core 0.

Upstream-Status: Pending [RustAmp]
